# How to add a compound component

> **Check rule `13-radix-primitives-first.mdc` before you start.** Radix UI almost certainly has a primitive for compound widgets like `AppModal`, `AppSheet`, `AppTabs`, `AppAccordion`, `AppDropdown`, `AppRadioGroup` — it handles the state machine, ARIA, keyboard navigation, and focus management for you. The pattern below is how to **wrap** a Radix primitive in this project's file layout, not how to rebuild one from scratch.

Pattern: a parent that owns (or wraps Radix-owned) state and shares it with named subcomponents. Use this for `AppModal`, `AppSheet`, `AppTabs`, `AppAccordion`, `AppDropdown`, `AppRadioGroup` — anything with named slots.

Every design-system component is prefixed `App` (see AGENTS.md Part 2 — Conventions). Examples below use `AppModal` as the canonical case; substitute `App<Name>` for your component.

For folder layout (extra files compared to a simple component), see AGENTS.md Part 2 (Conventions).

## Step-by-step (AppModal as the canonical example)

1. Create `src/components/AppModal/` with:

   ```
   AppModal/
   ├── index.tsx                    ← root, owns state, renders Context.Provider, attaches subcomponents
   ├── AppModal.Header.tsx          ← subcomponent, consumes context
   ├── AppModal.Body.tsx
   ├── AppModal.Footer.tsx
   ├── AppModal.context.ts          ← Context + useAppModalContext()
   ├── AppModal.types.ts
   ├── AppModal.module.scss         ← root + shared styles
   ├── AppModal.Header.module.scss
   ├── AppModal.Body.module.scss
   ├── AppModal.Footer.module.scss
   ├── AppModal.stories.tsx
   ├── README.md
   └── assets/                      ← only if colocated SVGs are needed
   ```

2. Context (`AppModal.context.ts`):

   ```ts
   import { createContext, useContext } from 'react'

   export type AppModalContextValue = {
     isOpen: boolean
     close: () => void
   }

   export const AppModalContext = createContext<AppModalContextValue | null>(null)

   export const useAppModalContext = (): AppModalContextValue => {
     const ctx = useContext(AppModalContext)
     if (!ctx) {
       throw new Error('AppModal subcomponents must be rendered inside <AppModal>.')
     }
     return ctx
   }
   ```

3. Root (`index.tsx`) — owns state, renders the provider, and attaches subcomponents onto the root for the compound API:

   ```tsx
   'use client'

   import { useCallback, useMemo } from 'react'
   import cn from 'classnames'

   import { AppModalContext } from './AppModal.context'
   import { AppModalHeader } from './AppModal.Header'
   import { AppModalBody } from './AppModal.Body'
   import { AppModalFooter } from './AppModal.Footer'

   import s from './AppModal.module.scss'

   import type { AppModalProps } from './AppModal.types'

   const AppModalRoot = ({ isOpen, onClose, className, children }: AppModalProps) => {
     const close = useCallback(() => onClose(), [onClose])
     const value = useMemo(() => ({ isOpen, close }), [isOpen, close])

     if (!isOpen) return null

     return (
       <AppModalContext.Provider value={value}>
         <div
           role="dialog"
           aria-modal="true"
           className={cn(s.root, className)}
         >
           {children}
         </div>
       </AppModalContext.Provider>
     )
   }

   type AppModalCompound = typeof AppModalRoot & {
     Header: typeof AppModalHeader
     Body: typeof AppModalBody
     Footer: typeof AppModalFooter
   }

   export const AppModal = AppModalRoot as AppModalCompound
   AppModal.Header = AppModalHeader
   AppModal.Body = AppModalBody
   AppModal.Footer = AppModalFooter

   export type { AppModalProps } from './AppModal.types'
   ```

4. Subcomponents (`AppModal.Header.tsx`, `AppModal.Body.tsx`, `AppModal.Footer.tsx`) are arrow-function components and call `useAppModalContext()` when they need shared state:

   ```tsx
   import cn from 'classnames'

   import { useAppModalContext } from './AppModal.context'

   import s from './AppModal.Header.module.scss'

   import type { AppModalHeaderProps } from './AppModal.types'

   export const AppModalHeader = ({ title, className }: AppModalHeaderProps) => {
     const { close } = useAppModalContext()
     return (
       <header className={cn(s.root, className)}>
         <h2 className={s.title}>{title}</h2>
         <button
           type="button"
           className={s.close}
           onClick={close}
           aria-label="Close"
         >
           ×
         </button>
       </header>
     )
   }
   ```

5. Consumers use the compound API:

   ```tsx
   <AppModal isOpen={isOpen} onClose={close}>
     <AppModal.Header title="Confirm booking" />
     <AppModal.Body>...</AppModal.Body>
     <AppModal.Footer>
       <AppButton variant="primary" onClick={confirm}>Confirm</AppButton>
     </AppModal.Footer>
   </AppModal>
   ```

## Notes

- Mark the root file `'use client'` whenever the component owns interactive state (`useState`, `useCallback`, etc.). Subcomponents that only render markup do not need the directive — they inherit the client boundary from the root.
- Each subcomponent gets its own `*.module.scss`. Shared layout styles live in `AppModal.module.scss`.
- Re-export from `src/components/index.ts` only the root and shared types — the compound members are accessed via `AppModal.Header`, `AppModal.Body`, etc.

## Stories, showcase, and barrel

Same Storybook + barrel + showcase entry steps as a simple component. See `10-add-simple-component.mdc` steps 5–9. Storybook title is `Components/AppModal`. Stories should cover the closed state, the open state, and any subcomponent permutation that meaningfully differs (header-only, header + body, full compound). Showcase slug stays unprefixed (`modal`); the `name` field in the catalog is `AppModal`.
